//? Title: Warshall closure: actual intermediate phases and positive-length cycles
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Boolean reachability grows by allowing one more intermediate vertex at a time.
Actual post-phase matrices and selected inner updates retain the original
three-vertex chain while exposing reflexive and cycle semantics.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Let R^(k)(i,j) denote a path whose intermediate vertices are below k. Then
R^(k+1)(i,j)=R^(k)(i,j) or(R^(k)(i,k) and R^(k)(k,j)). The native producer skips
an inner row when R(i,k) is false and counts the actual remaining j updates.
Worst-case time is cubic and bit storage quadratic. With reflexivefalse, the
result represents positive-length paths: cycles still reach their starting
vertices. It does not force a false diagonal.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/transitive_closure_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/transitive_closure.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::transitive_closure_trace(3, {{0, 1}, {1, 2}}, false);
    std::print("| actual allowed intermediate k | actual matrix after k | cumulative inner updates | actual " "new paths |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.phases)
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | {} | {} |\n", s.intermediate, s.after,
                   s.candidate_updates, s.new_paths);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual chain0->1->2, no reflexive seed");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual gated inner updates",
                                     r.candidate_updates));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual path0->2 {}",
                                     bool(r.reachable[0][2])));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/transitive_closure_tiny.svg");
}
```
