> API and interpretation

All endpoints and complete n-squared geometry are validated before allocation.
Self loops and duplicate edges are accepted, with seed assignments counted.
Actual matrix histories come from the producing k loop and have their own
complete-copy policy. Empty graphs are valid; theoretical worst-case cubic work
is distinct from actual gated counts.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Warshall, A Theorem on Boolean Matrices, JACM9 (1962),11-12|https://doi.org/10.1145/321105.321107]

